exports[`capability surfaces — minimal > help on chat 1`] = `
"*Switchboard* — send me a request. Agents:
• \`general\` — Default assistant on the configured model: answers directly, reads the org's repos and manages their issues over GitHub, reads URLs. No workspace or shell.
• \`coding\` — Implements changes and ships PRs (git + gh in a workspace).
• \`review\` — Reviews PRs and produces high-quality findings. Read-only.
• \`ship\` — Coding → review → fix pipeline to LGTM: opens the PR, loops reviews, reports merge-ready. Never merges.
• \`research\` — Answers questions with web search, URL reading, and read access to the org's repos and issues over GitHub. No workspace.

*Per-request directives* (anywhere in the message):
\`agent:review model:anthropic/claude-opus-5 effort:low look at PR 42\` (effort: low | medium | high — lower = faster turns)

*Commands* (\`<group> <verb> [args…] [--option value…]\`; \`<group> help\` lists a group, \`<group> <verb> --help\` explains one):
*help*
• \`help show\` — What Switchboard can do: agents, per-request directives, and every chat command.
*config*
• \`config show\` — The effective agent/model/effort for you in this channel, the defaults, both scopes, and what is restricted.
• \`config set\` — Set the agent, model, or effort for a channel (gated) or for yourself; per-agent forms take --models.<agent> / --efforts.<agent>.
• \`config clear\` — Drop every runtime override of a channel (gated) or of yourself; static config.yaml values show through again.
• \`config instructions\` — Custom instructions for a channel (gated) or for yourself — advisory prompt content that never changes agent, model, or permissions.
*runs*
• \`runs list\` — List runs (live and persisted, newest first) — metadata only, never message text.
• \`runs stop\` — Request a live run to stop (\`--mode soft\` = finish the current step; \`hard\` = abort now). Records the caller as the actor.
*repo*
• \`repo test\` — Run the repo's onboarded test command with zero model turns (needs coding-agent access; the ref must be a plausible branch).
• \`repo build\` — Run the repo's onboarded build command with zero model turns (needs coding-agent access; the ref must be a plausible branch).
*deploy*
• \`deploy plan\` — The production deploy plan: checks, Worker order, preflight handling — computed, nothing executed. With --affected, also which Workers this tree actually needs deployed and why."
`;

exports[`capability surfaces — minimal > self-description block (the resident cap is the Worker's answer — 6 where there is a fleet) 1`] = `
"About Switchboard (yourself): you are Switchboard, the agent gateway of the acme organization. A message arrives on a channel (Slack — an @-mention, thread follow-ups stay on the same agent — plus a CLI and an HTTP /api surface), is routed to an agent, runs on a configured provider/model, and executes tools through an executor.
Agents: \`general\` — Default assistant on the configured model: answers directly, reads the org's repos and manages their issues over GitHub, reads URLs. No workspace or shell.; \`coding\` — Implements changes and ships PRs (git + gh in a workspace).; \`review\` — Reviews PRs and produces high-quality findings. Read-only.; \`ship\` — Coding → review → fix pipeline to LGTM: opens the PR, loops reviews, reports merge-ready. Never merges.; \`research\` — Answers questions with web search, URL reading, and read access to the org's repos and issues over GitHub. No workspace.. Users pick one with an inline \`agent:<name>\` directive (default: general); \`model:\` / \`effort:\` ride the same way (see the runtime-config block).
Repos: this installation has no resident (always-warm) repo environments — the coding and review agents clone the repository a request names (an https://github.com/owner/name URL or a PR link) into a per-thread workspace on the bot host for the run. Nothing is kept warm between runs, and there is nothing to onboard.
Runs: every run (agent or operator command) has a live page under /runs with its events while it runs (this installation keeps no run history: a finished run's page goes away about a minute later); runs can be stopped from there. This installation has no cross-session memory: a run knows only its own thread. \`help\` lists every chat command.
Source of truth: the code lives in the GitHub repo coreplanelabs/switchboard — README.md (architecture + agents), AGENTS.md (invariants + map), and one behavioral spec per feature under docs/reference/specs/*.md (e.g. docs/reference/specs/resident-repos.md, docs/reference/specs/routing-and-config.md, docs/reference/specs/github-tools.md). For a question about how Switchboard works beyond this block, read those files with the GitHub tools when you have them (github_tree / github_file on coreplanelabs/switchboard) — they are private, so a public-web fetch 404s; if you have no GitHub tools, answer from this block and point at that path. Never describe yourself as stateless, tool-less by design, or unable to know your own workings."
`;

